Problem description:
[eSignet Performance & Memory Leak Audit Report.pdf](https://mosip.atlassian.net/browse/ES-2996)

Problem A — Same JWT String Parsed Multiple Times Per Request

In `DpopValidationFilter.java` (lines 154–168)

```// Inside isDpopBoundAccessToken() — parse #1
private boolean isDpopBoundAccessToken(String accessToken) {
    SignedJWT jwt = SignedJWT.parse(accessToken);
    // reads cnf claim from jwt
}

// Inside validateCnfClaim() — parse #2, same string
private void validateCnfClaim(JWK jwk, String accessToken) {
    SignedJWT jwt = SignedJWT.parse(accessToken);
    // validates cnf thumbprint
}
```

// Both are called from the same filter execution(`doFilterInternal`) — same accessToken string

```isDpopBoundAccessToken(accessToken); 
validateCnfClaim(jwk, accessToken);
```

The calling method passes the raw string down to both methods, each of which independently parses it. Neither method knows the other already did the same work.

Solution Suggested: 

```// DpopValidationFilter — parse once, reuse:
SignedJWT accessTokenJwt = SignedJWT.parse(accessToken);
boolean isDpopBound = isDpopBoundAccessToken(accessTokenJwt);
validateCnfClaim(jwk, accessTokenJwt);
```

In `TokenServiceImpl.java` (lines 172–192)

```// Line 172 — parse #1 
SignedJWT signedJWT = SignedJWT.parse(clientAssertion); 
String alg = signedJWT.getHeader().getAlgorithm().getName(); 
String sub = signedJWT.getJWTClaimsSet().getSubject(); 

// ... some code in between ...

 // Line 187 —jwtDecoder.decode() internally calls SignedJWT.parse() again — parse #2 
 jwtDecoder.decode(clientAssertion);
```

The `jwtDecoder.decode(clientAssertion)` call is the hidden culprit. Spring Security's `NimbusJwtDecoder.decode()` takes a raw String and internally calls `SignedJWT.parse()` again. It does not know you already have a parsed object sitting right there.

Solution: 

```// TokenServiceImpl — extract claims from already-parsed JWT:
SignedJWT signedJWT = SignedJWT.parse(clientAssertion);
// validate headers/claims from signedJWT directly
```

