[exalate-issue-sync[bot]]: Harsh Kashiwal commented: The C4 finding of redundant JWT parsing in DpopValidationFilter is a false positive. The original task description incorrectly assumed isDpopBoundAccessToken and validateCnfClaim execute in the same request flow, but they are in mutually exclusive branches. Each path parses the access token exactly once. No fix is warranted in this file.

For {{TokenServiceImpl.java}}, NimbusJwtDecoder requires alg as an argument which cannot be  fetched without parsing the clientAssertion and hence 
SignedJWT.parse() is unavoidable

{noformat}NimbusJwtDecoder jwtDecoder = getNimbusJwtDecoderFromJwk(jwk, clientId, audience, maxClockSkew, alg);
jwtDecoder.decode(clientAssertion);{noformat}

The only way to eliminate parse #2 would be to stop using {{jwtDecoder.decode()}} and verify the JWT signature manually using the Nimbus API directly — which is a significant architectural change

